        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-doryssus-early-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-doryssus-early-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.4e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-doryssus-early-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Schnakenberg Turing wavelength of Gasterosteus doryssus_early at 33 µm (10.02 Ma) — Model fidelity to source: 86/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The script integrates Schnakenberg kinetics and scores growth rates against the eigenvalue of J - k_eff² D (Pearson r = 0.9947 on 11 modes). D_u and the diffusion ratio are solved for λ near 32.86 µm rather than copied from the 2.3 mm sibling slot. Deductions: the GIF carrier is an imposed m=2 spiral, not a saturated spiral of the PDE (-8); a and b are not taken from a stickleback paper (-4); the successor wavelength is the same dispersion law with D_u rescaled, not a second integration (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-doryssus-early-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-doryssus-early-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-doryssus-early-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.6e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-doryssus-early-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Schnakenberg Turing wavelength of Gasterosteus doryssus_early at 33 µm (10.02 Ma) — Morphometric validation: 84/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Dispersion Pearson r = 0.9947, RMSE = 0.0259, KS = 0.182 against the discrete linear theory. Nonlinear λ = 33.87 µm versus 32.86 µm (3.1%). Specimen high-pass wavelength 81.08 µm, Otsu foreground 0.291, and coherency 0.198 are stored with references they do not equal. Deduction: no multi-seed CV of λ, and the specimen numbers are a mismatch report rather than a fitted wavelength (-6)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-doryssus-early-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-dispersion-pearson-r-of-analytic-vs-linearized-euler-growth>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-doryssus-early-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-dispersion-rmse>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-doryssus-early-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-equal-diffusion-ablation-std-ratio>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-doryssus-early-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-ks-statistic-of-standardized-dispersion-curves>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-doryssus-early-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-nonlinear-schnakenberg-selected-wavelength>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-doryssus-early-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-specimen-image-high-pass-radial-wavelength>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-doryssus-early-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-specimen-otsu-foreground-fraction>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-doryssus-early-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-specimen-structure-tensor-coherency>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-doryssus-early-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-specimen-vs-gif-cv-similarity>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-doryssus-early-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-successor-doryssus-mid-analytic-wavelength>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-doryssus-early-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-doryssus-early-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-doryssus-early-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.4e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-doryssus-early-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Schnakenberg Turing wavelength of Gasterosteus doryssus_early at 33 µm (10.02 Ma) — MorphoEval overall 84.5/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 1. Periodic Schnakenberg field on a 280 µm patch with D_u = 8.204 µm² and D_v/D_u = 12.277, chosen so argmax σ(k) sits at 33.01 µm against the assigned λ_c = 32.86 µm (3.286e-05 m) at 10.02 Ma. Nonlinear FFT wavelength 33.87 µm. Linearized dispersion Pearson r = 0.9947, RMSE = 0.0259, KS = 0.182. Equal-diffusion ablation std ratio 2.16e-4. D_u sweep is monotonic from 27.65 µm to 41.71 µm. Gallery ocellus high-pass band measures 81.08 µm and is reported as a different length. GIF CV similarity against that photograph is 85.9 (12 frames, 640×480). Successor doryssus_mid λ is analytic only (41.71 µm). Overall 84.5/100 (faithfulness 83.1, reproducibility 87.6); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d; environment: python 3.12.3, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.18.1, matplotlib 3.11.2, Pillow 13.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 86, Morphological realism / specimen match 80, Parameter expressivity 84, Morphometric validation 84, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 84, Reproducibility package 88. Output judged: docs/media/gasterosteus_doryssus_early_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-gasterosteus-doryssus-early-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d, image/png, 331153 B, 1512×984 px, artifact_sha256 d2172aa3837f97872586cc97d88a282113f4a76bbe3eb225414e55a1258b4d19 (sha256 d2172aa3837f97872586cc97d88a282113f4a76bbe3eb225414e55a1258b4d19), spec_fingerprint 7da029c4116b272894d7e1440005167263445ac99716f78586b6bac5b2bee85e. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 7da029c4116b272894d7e1440005167263445ac99716f78586b6bac5b2bee85e; artifact_sha256: d2172aa3837f97872586cc97d88a282113f4a76bbe3eb225414e55a1258b4d19. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing (1952) dispersion relation and the critical wavenumber of a two-species reaction-diffusion system. | Schnakenberg (1979) kinetics du/dt = a - u + u^2 v, dv/dt = b - u^2 v. | Hunt, Bell & Travis (2008) and Bell, Travis & Blouw (2006): Truckee Formation G. doryssus pelvic reduction over about 22 kyr, with a complete pelvis at the start of the series (10.02 Ma in this slot's chronology). | Stuart, Travis & Bell (2020): Pitx1 contributes to pelvic reduction in this fossil lineage. | Nakamasu et al. (2009) and Kondo & Miura (2010): teleost chromatophores can sit in a Turing regime.; reconstructed_in_script: A 96² explicit-Euler Schnakenberg integration on a 280 µm patch, a 11-mode linearized dispersion test, a six-point D_u sweep, and an equal-diffusion ablation. | An m=2 spiral ocellus whose amplitude follows RMS(u), rendered as a 12-frame 640×480 GIF calibrated to the gallery photograph's orientation and radial spectrum.; transfer_boundary: The 32.86 µm length is the Delphi cellular-detail assignment. Bell, Hunt, and Stuart did not publish a pigment spacing. | Nakamasu/Kondo zebrafish chromatophore kinetics are not re-fit; a=0.062 and b=0.948 are a Jacobian that places the fastest mode at this wavelength. | The gallery image is a project species-gallery spiral with a 100 µm scale bar, not a Truckee thin section.; does_not_claim: That the fossil pelvis was measured at 33 µm, that the gallery band of 81.08 µm equals λ_c, or that doryssus_mid was integrated as a second PDE on this pass.." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: R1: Integrate the successor (doryssus_mid) Schnakenberg field at D_u scaled by (41.50/32.86)^2 and report its FFT wavelength next to the analytic 41.71 µm. Pass 1 only evaluates the dispersion law.",
        "remediation needed: R2: Repeat the nonlinear 280 µm patch at four seeds and report the coefficient of variation of the selected wavelength.",
        "remediation needed: R3: Sweep the diffusion ratio D_v/D_u at fixed D_u. Pass 1 sweeps D_u only.",
        "remediation needed: R4: A second assessor from another provider has not scored this pass." ;
    pk:hasScore 8.45e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-doryssus-early-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Schnakenberg Turing wavelength of Gasterosteus doryssus_early at 33 µm (10.02 Ma) — Parameter expressivity: 84/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Raising D_u at fixed diffusion ratio lengthens λ monotonically from 27.65 µm through 33.01 µm to 41.71 µm, which is the early-to-mid chronospecies direction. Setting D_v = D_u drops the field std by a factor of about 4600 and makes every tested σ(k) negative. Deduction: the diffusion ratio itself is not swept, and the nonlinear patch is one seed (-6)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-doryssus-early-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-doryssus-early-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.4e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-doryssus-early-turing-wavelength-s0-repro-package> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Schnakenberg Turing wavelength of Gasterosteus doryssus_early at 33 µm (10.02 Ma) — Reproducibility package: 88/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Seed 3229, SHA-256 checks on the reference JSON, specimen, scout manifest, bib, and README, and a --self-test that asserts r > 0.98, ablation ratio < 0.05, monotonic sweep, GIF frames >= 10, and minimum side >= 480. The self-test passed (r = 0.9947, CV = 85.9, 12 frames, 640×480). Deduction: no per-script lock file beyond the environment recorded here (-6); Lean binary absent (-6, shared with code-traceability, counted once here as -4 for the missing checker only)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-repro-package> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
